{
  "$comment": "ADR-113 Amendment 4 fixture. JSON-RPC 2.0 POSTed to the daemon's OAuth listener with a bearer token, exactly as kb/query.* is. Clients branch on error.data.kind only; error.code is informative. Identifiers, hashes and times are examples; times are RFC 3339 UTC with milliseconds. Field names and kinds are normative.",
  "method": "kb/review.events",
  "description": "The KB's event chain, paged, owner and auditor only (it names principals). Each line is an export line (Amendment 4 E10): `canonical` is the base64 of the event's RFC 8785 bytes, entry_hash = SHA-256(\"maereview/v1\\n\" || canonical), sig = Ed25519(daemon key, \"maereview-sig/v1\\n\" || entry_hash raw 32 bytes), and prev_hash is the previous line's entry_hash (64 zeros for seq 1). THESE FIXTURES VERIFY: they are signed with a fixed TEST key (seed bytes 0x01..0x20), whose public key is `header.daemon_key`. A real verifier takes the daemon key from an out-of-band anchor, never from the export.",
  "transport": {
    "http": "POST /",
    "headers": {
      "Authorization": "Bearer <the person's IdP access token for this daemon's audience>",
      "Content-Type": "application/json"
    }
  },
